<body><h1>ANSWER KEY — Set 6  <em>(grader only)</em></h1>
<p>Rubric per question: <strong>Route/action (4) · Policy stated (3) · Trap avoided (3)</strong> unless noted.</p>
<hr>
<p><strong>Q1 — Shipped but tracking shows no info.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Tracking / order status. <strong>Action:</strong> Explain the order has <strong>departed our warehouse and is in transit to UPS</strong> for final delivery; the tracking number is generated but <strong>won't display movement until UPS scans it</strong>. Provide the UPS link; if no update within <strong>2–3 business days</strong> after the expected hand-off, contact us.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> promising a hard delivery date, or saying it's lost. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q2 — Rush + shipping refund.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Expedite → Refund (goodwill). <strong>Action:</strong> Two parts: (1) we do <strong>not</strong> offer expedited shipping — explain and quote the timeline; (2) a shipping-cost refund for the delay is a <strong>goodwill gesture needing internal approval</strong> — don't promise it outright; escalate, and if approved advise the timing.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> promising either the rush or the shipping refund on the spot. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q3 — Bag/equipment defect.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Damaged/Defective (equipment). <strong>Action:</strong> Request <strong>photos</strong> of the damage; use the quality opener. A bag/equipment replacement may require <strong>internal (DM) approval</strong> before the replacement order is created. Replace same item/size.</li><li><strong>Trap (auto-fail):</strong> promising the replacement with no photo; or naming the internal approver (Dan/DM) to the customer. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q4 — Shipping refund on a return.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Return/Exchange. <strong>Action:</strong> Explain that <strong>return shipping costs are not refunded</strong> — Capelli is not responsible for refunding shipping costs. Refund is for the item's value once received (within policy).</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> telling them shipping will be refunded on a standard return. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q5 — Goodwill shipping refund (delay).</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Refund request (goodwill). <strong>Action:</strong> For an <strong>excessive delay</strong>, a shipping-cost refund is a goodwill gesture <strong>requiring internal approval</strong>. Acknowledge the specific delay; escalate; once approved advise ~24h to process (3–5 business days to appear). Own the follow-up rather than looping holds.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> promising the refund before approval. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q6 — Guest checkout, can't see order / order individual.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Account &amp; login (guest). <strong>Action:</strong> Explain that no account exists yet, so they can't view order status or order individual items. Ask them to <strong>create an account</strong> at the create-account link using the <strong>same email</strong> as the order; once created, we can <strong>link the order</strong> so they can order individual items. Confirm back when done.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> promising individual-item ordering without the account/link step. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q7 — Number shows old (club-controlled).</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Player link / order change (roster). <strong>Action:</strong> Player <strong>numbers/roster are entered by the club admin</strong>, not Capelli — we can't change it on our side. Direct the customer (ideally CC the club) to have the <strong>club update the roster</strong>; then order with the correct number.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> promising to change the number yourself. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q8 — OOS, flexible on color.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Out of stock (alt color). <strong>Action:</strong> Confirm the size is OOS with no firm restock date; offer the <strong>same item/size in an alternative color</strong> if available (or wait / cancel+refund). Confirm before shipping an alternative.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> shipping an alternative without confirmation, or promising a restock date. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q9 — Spot the mistake.</strong> Full credit = all caught (≈2.5 each):</p>
<ol><li><strong>Names internal contacts</strong> ("emailed GT and RI in planning") — never surface internal names/teams.</li><li><strong>Leaks internal system term</strong> ("OBD status") — internal fulfillment reference.</li><li><strong>Leaks internal process</strong> ("once the wave releases") — internal.</li><li><strong>Internal instruction sent to customer</strong> ("please don't reply") — that's an internal note, not customer-facing.</li></ol>
<ul><li><strong>Corrected message:</strong> acknowledge you're checking on the order status with the fulfillment center and will update them within 2–3 business days — none of the internal detail; keep internal notes internal. <em>(10)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q10 — Missing item → refund.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Missing item → Refund request. <strong>Action:</strong> Confirm the missing line item (white hat) against the order. Normally we ship the missing item; since the customer now prefers a <strong>refund</strong>, process the refund for that item (per policy/approval) rather than reshipping. Refund posts in 3–5 business days as "CAPELLI SPORT."</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> ignoring the refund request and reshipping anyway, or refunding without confirming the item was actually missing. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<hr>
